    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceTest` (3 tests) is the full test suite \u2014 `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper. **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional, validated-when-present `postcode` field end to end:\n\n**Contract / DTOs**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added `postcode` to the `OwnerFields` schema (optional, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`). Because `Owner` is `allOf OwnerFields`, the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response) both gain `postcode`. The 4-digit `@Pattern` makes a malformed value (`\"12\"`) fail bean validation \u2192 the existing `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 path, and keeps it absent-friendly.\n\n**Persistence**\n- `Owner` entity \u2014 new `postcode` field with `@Column(name = \"postcode\")` + getter/setter.\n- Added a nullable `postcode` column to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files (tests run on **hsqldb** with `ddl-auto=none`, so this was required; seed `data.sql` uses explicit column lists so it's unaffected). MapStruct maps `postcode` automatically by name in both directions.\n\n**Region-range rule** (spec: NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown region accepts any 4-digit)\n- New `Postcodes` util validating against the fixed city\u2192region table; a blank/absent postcode and unknown-region cities are no-ops.\n- New checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` (400, `errors: [\"postcode\"]`) + escalation YAML, following the existing telephone/email pattern.\n- Wired into `BuildOwner` (POST) and `ApplyOwner` (PUT), which also now copies `postcode`.\n\nResult on the three acceptance tests: valid postcode stored & echoed at `$.postcode`, owner without a postcode still accepted (2xx), malformed postcode rejected with 400.",
